[2026-03-14T20:56:46.849Z] {"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"abe1180e24abf8ccb","tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3uzCzrC4cut7RY3uYSZ3w","description":"Reading skills/scripts/seed-db.md","usage":{"total_tokens":17243,"tool_uses":4,"duration_ms":1590},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"ab1af0d2-a76e-48e1-afe8-7831ed7f3b5f","session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b"}
[2026-03-14T20:56:46.850Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNMQPXKJW3AocZM4mQEVSc","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# deploy\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Creates and/or syncs the production Neon database and creates and/or updates the Netlify site.\n     6→This is the single command for deploying the app to production. All project information\n     7→(database URL, Netlify site ID, etc.) is persisted in `.env` so subsequent runs reuse existing\n     8→resources.\n     9→\n    10→## Usage\n    11→\n    12→- `package.json` entry: `\"deploy\": \"tsx scripts/deploy.ts\"`\n    13→- No command-line arguments.\n    14→- Example: `npm run deploy`\n    15→\n    16→## Behavior\n    17→\n    18→### Database setup (first run)\n    19→\n    20→1. Check `.env` for an existing `NEON_PROJECT_ID`. If not present:\n    21→   a. Create a new Neon project via the Neon API.\n    22→   b. Write `NEON_PROJECT_ID` and `DATABASE_URL` to `.env`.\n    23→\n    24→### Database schema sync (every run)\n    25→\n    26→2. Call `initSchema(productionDatabaseUrl)` to create any missing tables.\n    27→3. Run migrations (`migrate-db` logic) against the production database to handle `ALTER TABLE`\n    28→   changes that `initSchema` cannot detect.\n    29→\n    30→### Seed data (first deployment only)\n    31→\n    32→4. On the **first deployment** (i.e. the database was just created), insert seed data that\n    33→   demonstrates the app's features. The seed data should be realistic and cover the main\n    34→   entities and relationships so a user can immediately explore the app without needing to\n    35→   create everything from scratch. Skip seeding on subsequent deployments.\n    36→\n    37→### Netlify site setup (first run)\n    38→\n    39→5. Check `.env` for an existing `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`. If not present:\n    40→   a. Create a new Netlify site via `netlify sites:create`.\n    41→   b. Write `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` to `.env`.\n    42→\n    43→### Build and deploy (every run)\n    44→\n    45→6. Build the app (`vite build`). Pipe build output to the log file.\n    46→7. Deploy to Netlify (`netlify deploy --prod`). Pipe deploy output to the log file.\n    47→8. Write the deployed URL, `site_id`, `neon_project_id`, and `database_url` to the top of `deployment.txt`\n    48→   (overwriting the previous resource block but preserving any deployment history entries below).\n    49→9. Print a one-line summary to stdout:\n    50→   - Success: `Deployed to <url>`\n    51→   - Failure: `Deploy failed (build|netlify) — see logs/deploy.log`\n    52→\n    53→## Populating `.env` for Redeployments\n    54→\n    55→`.env` is gitignored and will not exist in a fresh environment. If the app has been\n    56→deployed before, you MUST populate `.env` before running the script so it reuses the\n    57→existing Netlify site and Neon database instead of creating new ones.\n    58→\n    59→Read `deployment.txt` (committed to git) to get all previously stored deployment\n    60→values (`site_id`, `neon_project_id`, `database_url`). Write them to `.env`:\n    61→\n    62→```\n    63→NETLIFY_SITE_ID=<site_id from deployment.txt>\n    64→NEON_PROJECT_ID=<neon_project_id from deployment.txt>\n    65→DATABASE_URL=<database_url from deployment.txt>\n    66→```\n    67→\n    68→If `.env` is missing these values the script will create **new** resources, which means\n    69→a new URL and an empty database. Always check `deployment.txt` first.\n    70→\n    71→## Inputs\n    72→\n    73→- **Environment variables**:\n    74→  - `NEON_API_KEY` (required): For Neon project/database management.\n    75→  - `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` (required): For Netlify CLI authentication.\n    76→  - `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` (required): For Netlify site creation.\n    77→- **Files**:\n    78→  - `.env`: Read for existing project info (`NEON_PROJECT_ID`, `DATABASE_URL`,\n    79→    `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`). Written to on first run.\n    80→  - `deployment.txt`: Resource block at the top contains `site_id`, `neon_project_id`, and\n    81→    `database_url` from the last deployment (committed to git). Use this to populate `.env`\n    82→    when deploying in a fresh environment. Deployment history entries follow below.\n    83→\n    84→## Outputs\n    85→\n    86→- **stdout**: One-line summary only.\n    87→- **`logs/deploy.log`**: Full build and deploy output. Overwritten each run.\n    88→- **`.env`**: Updated with `NEON_PROJECT_ID`, `DATABASE_URL`, `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` if created.\n    89→- **`deployment.txt`**: Resource block at the top is updated with the current deployed URL,\n    90→  `site_id`, `neon_project_id`, and `database_url`. Deployment history entries below the\n    91→  resource block are preserved. The deployment skill appends a new history entry after\n    92→  each successful deploy.\n    93→- **Side effects**:\n    94→  - Creates Neon project (first run only).\n    95→  - Syncs production database schema (every run).\n    96→  - Creates Netlify site (first run only).\n    97→  - Deploys built app to Netlify (every run).\n    98→- **Exit codes**:\n    99→  - 0: Deployment succeeded.\n   100→  - Non-zero: A step failed.\n   101→\n   102→## SPA Routing\n   103→\n   104→Single-page apps require a `_redirects` file so that Netlify serves `index.html` for all\n   105→client-side routes. Without this, direct navigation to `/dashboard` or other routes returns 404.\n   106→\n   107→Create `public/_redirects` with:\n   108→\n   109→```\n   110→/* /index.html 200\n   111→```\n   112→\n   113→The deploy script should ensure this file exists before building. If the app uses client-side\n   114→routing (React Router, etc.), this file is mandatory.\n   115→\n   116→## Post-Deploy Checklist\n   117→\n   118→After the first successful deployment, verify that required environment variables are set on\n   119→the Netlify site. Missing env vars cause production 500 errors that are hard to diagnose.\n   120→\n   121→**IMPORTANT: Check for account-level env var overrides.** Netlify account-level environment\n   122→variables take precedence over site-level variables. If `DATABASE_URL` is set at the account\n   123→level, it will override the site-level value, causing the production app to connect to the\n   124→wrong database. To check and fix:\n   125→\n   126→```bash\n   127→# Check account-level env vars\n   128→curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n   129→  \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/$NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG/env\" | python3 -c \"\n   130→import sys, json\n   131→for v in json.load(sys.stdin):\n   132→    print(v['key'], '=', v['values'][0]['value'][:20] if v['values'] else '(empty)')\n   133→\"\n   134→\n   135→# If DATABASE_URL exists at account level, delete or override it at site level\n   136→# Use context \"production\" (not \"all\") when setting site-level overrides\n   137→curl -s -X PATCH -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n   138→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   139→  \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/$NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG/env/DATABASE_URL\" \\\n   140→  -d '{\"context\":\"production\",\"value\":\"<correct-database-url>\"}'\n   141→```\n   142→\n   143→Use the Netlify REST API to set environment variables — the CLI `npx netlify env:set --site`\n   144→flag is unreliable and silently fails in many environments. See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`\n   145→for the working REST API approach.\n   146→\n   147→1. **Check existing env vars**: Use the Netlify REST API or `LC_ALL=C npx netlify env:list --json --site $NETLIFY_SITE_ID`\n   148→2. **Set `DATABASE_URL`**: See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md` for the REST API command.\n   149→   The deploy script writes `DATABASE_URL` to `.env` but does NOT automatically set it on Netlify.\n   150→   You must set it manually after the first deploy.\n   151→3. **Run the deployment test** (`npx playwright test --config playwright.deployment.config.ts`)\n   152→   to confirm the production app can load data and perform writes.\n   153→\n   154→## Exporting `.env` for Shell Commands\n   155→\n   156→`source .env` does NOT export variables — they are only available in the current shell, not in\n   157→subprocesses or `curl` commands. When you need `.env` values in shell commands, use:\n   158→\n   159→```bash\n   160→export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)\n   161→```\n   162→\n   163→This exports all non-comment lines as environment variables accessible to subprocesses.\n   164→\n   165→## Locale Workaround\n   166→\n   167→The Netlify CLI requires a valid locale. In containers that lack `en_US.UTF-8`, CLI commands\n   168→(`netlify deploy`, `netlify sites:create`) fail with locale errors. Always prefix Netlify CLI\n   169→commands with `LC_ALL=C` to avoid this:\n   170→\n   171→```bash\n   172→LC_ALL=C npx netlify deploy --prod --dir dist --functions ./netlify/functions\n   173→LC_ALL=C npx netlify sites:create --account-slug $NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG\n   174→```\n   175→\n   176→The deploy script should set `LC_ALL=C` in the environment before spawning Netlify CLI\n   177→subprocesses.\n   178→\n   179→**ANSI code contamination**: `LC_ALL=C` also prevents ANSI escape codes from appearing in\n   180→CLI output. Without it, extracting URLs or site IDs from `netlify deploy` output may capture\n   181→embedded escape sequences that corrupt `.env` values and break subsequent `curl` calls. See\n   182→`skills/scripts/deploy-troubleshooting.md` for details.\n   183→\n   184→## Netlify CLI Troubleshooting\n   185→\n   186→The Netlify CLI (`npx netlify`) can fail in container environments. Common issues:\n   187→\n   188→- **Locale errors**: Always prefix with `LC_ALL=C` (see Locale Workaround above).\n   189→- **`npx netlify` not found or crashes**: Verify `netlify-cli` is installed:\n   190→  `ls node_modules/.bin/netlify 2>/dev/null || npm install netlify-cli --save-dev`\n   191→- **Direct invocation fails**: If `npx netlify` fails, try the full path:\n   192→  `./node_modules/.bin/netlify deploy --prod ...`\n   193→- **Both invocation methods fail**: The CLI may not be installed globally or locally. Install\n   194→  it explicitly: `npm install netlify-cli --save-dev`, then use `npx netlify`.\n   195→- **Interactive prompts** (CRITICAL): Netlify CLI commands like `netlify sites:create` will\n   196→  prompt interactively for missing arguments (e.g., site name), which hangs in non-interactive\n   197→  shells. The deploy script must NEVER produce interactive prompts. Always pass required\n   198→  arguments explicitly (e.g., `--name <site-name>` or `--site <site-id>`). Test the script\n   199→  end-to-end in a non-interactive shell before considering it complete.\n   200→- **Authentication errors**: Verify `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` is set:\n   201→  `echo $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN | head -c 5`\n   202→- **\"Site not found\" errors on deploy**: If `netlify deploy` fails with a site-not-found error,\n   203→  run `npx netlify link --id $NETLIFY_SITE_ID` before deploying. This writes the site ID to\n   204→  `.netlify/state.json`, which the CLI reads to identify the target site. The site ID can be\n   205→  found in `.env` (`NETLIFY_SITE_ID`) or `deployment.txt` (`site_id`).\n   206→\n   207→All Netlify CLI commands in the deploy script should use `LC_ALL=C` and pipe output to the\n   208→log file rather than inheriting stdio.\n   209→\n   210→## Database Schema Execution\n   211→\n   212→When running schema scripts directly (outside the deploy script), use `npx tsx -e` with an\n   213→inline import rather than `npx tsx scripts/schema.ts`. The direct file invocation has known\n   214→module resolution issues with `@neondatabase/serverless`:\n   215→\n   216→```bash\n   217→# This often fails with module resolution errors:\n   218→npx tsx scripts/schema.ts\n   219→\n   220→# This works reliably:\n   221→npx tsx -e \"import { initSchema } from './scripts/schema.ts'; await initSchema(process.env.DATABASE_URL!);\"\n   222→```\n   223→\n   224→The deploy script handles this internally, but if you need to run schema operations manually\n   225→(e.g., during initial setup or debugging), use the inline import pattern.\n   226→\n   227→## JSON Parsing in Shell\n   228→\n   229→**`jq` is not available in the container.** When you need to parse JSON from shell commands\n   230→(e.g., Neon API responses, Netlify CLI output), use `node -e` or `python3 -c` instead.\n   231→Example:\n   232→\n   233→```bash\n   234→curl -s ... | node -e \"process.stdin.on('data',d=>console.log(JSON.parse(d).key))\"\n   235→```\n   236→\n   237→## Implementation Tips\n   238→\n   239→- Reuse `initSchema` from `scripts/schema.ts` for schema sync.\n   240→- Reuse migration logic from `scripts/migrate-db.ts`.\n   241→- Use the Neon REST API (`https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/...`) with `NEON_API_KEY` for\n   242→  project creation. Example:\n   243→  ```bash\n   244→  curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n   245→    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   246→    -d '{\"project\":{\"name\":\"my-app\"}}' \\\n   247→    https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects\n   248→  ```\n   249→- When running one-off database queries with `node -e`, use `--input-type=module` for ESM\n   250→  packages like `@neondatabase/serverless`:\n   251→  ```bash\n   252→  node --input-type=module -e \"import { neon } from '@neondatabase/serverless'; const sql = neon('...'); const r = await sql\\`SELECT 1\\`; console.log(r);\"\n   253→  ```\n   254→  Do NOT use `require()` with ESM-only packages — it will fail.\n   255→- Use `netlify sites:create --account-slug $NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` for site creation.\n   256→- Use `netlify deploy --prod --dir dist --functions ./netlify/functions` for deployment.\n   257→  If available, use `--json` to get machine-readable output that avoids ANSI escape code\n   258→  parsing issues.\n   259→- After deployment, verify the site URL returns 200 before proceeding to tests:\n   260→  ```bash\n   261→  curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" <deployed-url>\n   262→  ```\n   263→- Do NOT inherit stdio from subprocesses. Pipe all subprocess output to `logs/deploy.log`.\n   264→- Read/write `.env` using `fs` — parse as key=value lines, append new entries, don't\n   265→  clobber existing values.\n   266→- Production builds must use `sourcemap: true`, `minify: false`, and the React development\n   267→  bundle (see `vite.config.ts` settings) so Replay recordings show readable source.\n   268→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3uzCzrC4cut7RY3uYSZ3w","session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b","uuid":"818e8429-6fd6-41bf-bef7-8474aad7e47d"}
[2026-03-14T20:56:46.858Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01N3WEFDCg6VZ4prRkLHsn15","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013S6djjpUUura2VBtib3rdH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/skills/scripts/test.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":15651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1574,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3uzCzrC4cut7RY3uYSZ3w","session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b","uuid":"c22e6263-290d-4236-8c8c-32ffb48785e0"}
[2026-03-14T20:56:46.859Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013S6djjpUUura2VBtib3rdH","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# test\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Runs Playwright tests for a single test file using the Replay browser, with automatic Neon\n     6→branch setup, seeding, and failed-recording upload. This is the single entry point for running\n     7→tests during development and debugging.\n     8→\n     9→## Usage\n    10→\n    11→- `package.json` entry: `\"test\": \"tsx scripts/test.ts\"`\n    12→- Required argument: a test file path (e.g., `npm run test tests/clients-list-page.spec.ts`).\n    13→- Example: `npm run test tests/auth.spec.ts`\n    14→- **Always use `npm run test`**, never `npx tsx scripts/test.ts` directly. Direct `tsx` invocation\n    15→  fails on module resolution for `@neondatabase/serverless` and other dependencies. The `npm run`\n    16→  wrapper sets up the correct resolution context.\n    17→\n    18→## Pre-Flight\n    19→\n    20→Before running `npm run test`, follow the pre-flight checklist in `skills/scripts/preflight.md`.\n    21→In particular, always use `npx replayio install` (NOT `npx playwright install chromium`) for\n    22→browser setup — the Replay browser installs to `~/.replay/runtimes/` and does not require\n    23→the Playwright browsers path workaround.\n    24→\n    25→**Quick pre-checks** (these address the most common test failure causes):\n    26→1. Kill stale dev servers: `pkill -f \"netlify dev\" 2>/dev/null; pkill -f \"vite\" 2>/dev/null`\n    27→2. Verify dependencies: `ls node_modules/.package-lock.json` — if missing, run `npm install`.\n    28→3. Run with a timeout mindset: if a test hangs, it's likely a stale process or port conflict,\n    29→   not a test bug.\n    30→\n    31→**Note**: The test script already handles process cleanup (step 1 of Behavior) and recording\n    32→cleanup (step 6) internally. You do NOT need to run these pre-flight steps separately before\n    33→every `npm run test` invocation — only run the full pre-flight checklist once per test session\n    34→to verify env vars, Replay browser, and dependencies. Re-running pre-flight checks before\n    35→every individual test file wastes significant time.\n    36→\n    37→## Behavior\n    38→\n    39→1. **Kill stale processes**: Kill any leftover `netlify` or `vite` dev server processes from\n    40→   previous runs. Always suppress errors to avoid spurious failures when no process is running:\n    41→   `pkill -f \"netlify dev\" 2>/dev/null || true; pkill -f \"vite\" 2>/dev/null || true`\n    42→\n    43→2. **Clean up stale Neon branches**: List existing Neon branches and delete any that match the\n    44→   test branch naming convention (e.g., `test-run-*`) from interrupted previous runs.\n    45→\n    46→3. **Create ephemeral Neon branch**: Create a fresh branch from the project's main branch for\n    47→   this test run. Name it with a convention like `test-run-{timestamp}`.\n    48→\n    49→4. **Initialize and seed**: Run `initSchema` on the new branch, then run migrations, then seed\n    50→   test data.\n    51→\n    52→5. **Start `netlify dev`**: Start a single `netlify dev` instance with `DATABASE_URL` pointing\n    53→   to the ephemeral branch.\n    54→\n    55→6. **Remove stale recordings**: Run `npx replayio remove --all` to clear local recordings from\n    56→   prior runs.\n    57→\n    58→7. **Run Playwright**: Run `npx playwright test <testFile>` with `--retries 0 --workers 1`\n    59→   against the specified test file. Tests run serially, one at a time. The database is reset\n    60→   (truncate all tables and re-seed) between each test. Pipe all Playwright output to a log\n    61→   file (see Outputs).\n    62→\n    63→8. **Parse results**: Count passed/failed/skipped tests from the Playwright JSON reporter output\n    64→   at `test-results/results.json`.\n    65→\n    66→9. **On failure** (non-zero exit code):\n    67→   a. Parse `~/.replay/recordings.log` with a built-in parser (NOT `npx replayio list --json`,\n    68→      which crashes on large suites). The log is newline-delimited JSON with `kind` field:\n    69→      `createRecording`, `addMetadata`, `writeStarted`, `writeFinished`, etc.\n    70→   b. Append full metadata for every recording that has test metadata to the log file in a\n    71→      delimited block:\n    72→      ```\n    73→      === REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\n    74→      {\"id\":\"...\",\"testResult\":\"failed\",\"testTitle\":\"...\",\"specFile\":\"...\"}\n    75→      ...\n    76→      === END REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\n    77→      ```\n    78→   c. Upload exactly ONE recording: among all finished recordings where\n    79→      `metadata.test.result` is `\"failed\"` or `\"timedOut\"`, pick the one with the longest\n    80→      duration (the real recording, not zero-duration stubs). Upload with\n    81→      `npx replayio upload <id>`. On success, append `REPLAY UPLOADED: <recordingId>` to the\n    82→      log file. On failure, log the exit code.\n    83→\n    84→10. **Clean up**: Stop the `netlify dev` server. Delete the ephemeral Neon branch. Remove local\n    85→    recordings with `npx replayio remove --all`.\n    86→\n    87→11. **Print summary** to stdout: a single line like `10 passed` or\n    88→    `8 passed, 2 failed — see logs/test-run-3.log`. Include the uploaded recording ID\n    89→    if one was uploaded: `8 passed, 2 failed (recording: abc123) — see logs/test-run-3.log`.\n    90→\n    91→12. **Exit** with the original Playwright exit code.\n    92→\n    93→## Inputs\n    94→\n    95→- **Required argument**: Test file path (e.g., `tests/auth.spec.ts`).\n    96→- **Environment variables**:\n    97→  - `NEON_API_KEY` (required): For Neon branch management.\n    98→  - `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` (required): For Replay recording uploads.\n    99→  - `NEON_PROJECT_ID` (required): Read from `.env`. The Neon project to branch from.\n   100→  - `DATABASE_URL` (required): Read from `.env`. The main branch connection string used as\n   101→    template for ephemeral branches.\n   102→  - `REPLAY_CLI` (optional): Override the Replay CLI command (default: `replayio`, assumed\n   103→    globally installed). Useful for pointing at a local build or alternate installation.\n   104→- **Files**:\n   105→  - `.env`: Project configuration (Neon project ID, database URL, etc.).\n   106→  - `~/.replay/recordings.log`: Replay recording metadata (read after test run).\n   107→\n   108→## Outputs\n   109→\n   110→- **stdout**: One-line summary only. Never verbose test output.\n   111→- **`logs/test-run-N.log`**: Full Playwright output, recording metadata, and upload results.\n   112→  `N` increments each run (find the highest existing number and add 1).\n   113→- **Side effects**:\n   114→  - Creates and deletes ephemeral Neon branches.\n   115→  - Uploads failed Replay recordings.\n   116→  - Removes local recording files.\n   117→- **Exit codes**:\n   118→  - 0: All tests passed.\n   119→  - Non-zero: Test failures (matches Playwright's exit code).\n   120→\n   121→## Reading Test Results\n   122→\n   123→Always determine pass/fail status from the log file (`logs/test-run-N.log`) or\n   124→`test-results/results.json` — **never from stdout**. The Playwright output format combined\n   125→with Replay recording can show \"0 tests\" on stdout even when tests actually ran and passed.\n   126→This misleading output has caused repeated wasted investigation. If stdout says \"0 tests\",\n   127→check the log file before concluding that tests didn't run.\n   128→\n   129→## Parsing Test Failures\n   130→\n   131→The JSON log reporter strips test names and error details from `test-results/results.json`,\n   132→making it unreliable for identifying which tests failed. Do NOT spend time trying to parse\n   133→`results.json` with grep, python3, or node scripts — the data is not there.\n   134→\n   135→Instead, use this approach in order:\n   136→\n   137→1. **Check `test-results/*/error-context.md` files** — these contain readable failure details\n   138→   including test names and error messages. This is the fastest way to identify failures.\n   139→2. **Check `test-results/.last-run.json`** — provides high-level pass/fail status.\n   140→3. **Use Replay MCP tools** — if error-context files are insufficient, inspect the uploaded\n   141→   recording to diagnose the root cause. This is consistently the most effective approach\n   142→   for understanding failures.\n   143→\n   144→## Test Retry Limits\n   145→\n   146→When a test fails, do not blindly retry more than 3 times. After 3 failed runs, stop and\n   147→investigate the root cause rather than hoping for a different result. Common reasons for\n   148→persistent failures:\n   149→- **ECONNREFUSED on port 8888**: The dev server has a port conflict from a stale process,\n   150→  not a transient error. Kill stale processes (`pkill -f \"netlify dev\" 2>/dev/null; pkill -f \"vite\" 2>/dev/null`)\n   151→  and verify the port is free before retrying. Do not retry the test without clearing the port.\n   152→- **Assertion mismatches repeating identically**: The test or app has a bug — retrying won't help.\n   153→- **Timeouts on the same step**: Usually a stale process or resource issue, not flakiness.\n   154→\n   155→## Timeout-Prone Tests\n   156→\n   157→When tests consistently time out under the Replay Chromium browser (which adds 2–3x overhead),\n   158→use `test.slow()` at the top of the test body to triple Playwright's default timeout. This is\n   159→preferable to increasing `actionTimeout` globally, since it only affects known slow tests.\n   160→\n   161→## Standard Test Execution Pattern\n   162→\n   163→Follow this iterative pattern when running tests. This is the proven approach across 100+\n   164→worker iterations:\n   165→\n   166→1. **Pre-flight**: Follow `skills/scripts/preflight.md` (kill stale processes, verify env,\n   167→   clear recordings). Do this once per test session, not before every individual run.\n   168→2. **Run tests**: `npm run test tests/<spec-file>.spec.ts`\n   169→3. **On failure**: Read `test-results/*/error-context.md` files to identify which tests\n   170→   failed and why. Do NOT re-run without understanding the failure.\n   171→4. **Fix and re-run**: Fix the identified issue in app or test code, then re-run.\n   172→5. **Maximum 3 retries**: If the same test fails 3 times, stop and investigate the root\n   173→   cause rather than hoping for a different result. Use Replay MCP tools on the uploaded\n   174→   recording for deeper analysis.\n   175→6. **When to file a bug vs. keep fixing**: If the failure is in test code (wrong selector,\n   176→   hardcoded count, missing await), fix it. If the failure reveals an app bug that requires\n   177→   significant refactoring, file it as a bug report and move on.\n   178→\n   179→## Test Writing Guidelines\n   180→\n   181→For guidance on writing robust tests that work with this test script, see:\n   182→\n   183→- `skills/tasks/build/writeTests.md` § \"Test Design and Database Isolation\" — `beforeEach`\n   184→  cleanup hooks, relative assertions, and `data-testid` selector best practices.\n   185→- `skills/tasks/build/writeTests.md` § \"Directives\" — test isolation mandates including no\n   186→  hardcoded row counts, unique entity names, and `:not()` filters for prefix selectors.\n   187→\n   188→## Implementation Tips\n   189→\n   190→- Reuse `initSchema` from `scripts/schema.ts` and the seed logic from `scripts/seed-db.ts`.\n   191→- Use the Neon API directly (`fetch` to `https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/...`) for branch\n   192→  creation and deletion. The API key is `NEON_API_KEY`.\n   193→- Parse `~/.replay/recordings.log` in TypeScript — it's newline-delimited JSON. The\n   194→  `addMetadata` entries contain `metadata.test.result` which indicates pass/fail.\n   195→- The Playwright config must use the Replay browser via `replayDevices['Replay Chromium']`\n   196→  from `@replayio/playwright` and include `replayReporter` with `upload: false`.\n   197→- The HTML reporter must use `open: 'never'` to suppress the interactive \"Serving HTML report\"\n   198→  prompt that blocks the script from exiting.\n   199→- Run Playwright with `--retries 0 --workers 1` — no retries, no parallelism. Failures must\n   200→  be analyzed via Replay.\n   201→- Do NOT inherit stdio from Playwright. Pipe stdout and stderr to the log file using\n   202→  `child_process.execSync` with `stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe']` or similar, then write\n   203→  the captured output to the log file.\n   204→- Use the JSON reporter (`test-results/results.json`) to parse pass/fail counts for the\n   205→  summary line.\n   206→- The `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` env var is already set in the container.\n   207→- Reset the database between tests by truncating all app tables and re-running the seed script.\n   208→  This ensures each test starts with a clean, known dataset. Use `truncateAndSeed` (truncate\n   209→  all tables then seed) rather than just `seedDatabase` — Neon branches inherit data from their\n   210→  parent branch, and tests accumulate data across runs. Without truncation, tests see unexpected\n   211→  rows from prior runs or inherited branch data, which is the #1 cause of test failures.\n   212→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3uzCzrC4cut7RY3uYSZ3w","session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b","uuid":"12d29b41-3e07-49dd-b286-0804bb8917ad"}
[2026-03-14T20:56:46.859Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01N3WEFDCg6VZ4prRkLHsn15","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RTUdsbLy38mamUUT1Ythyt","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/skills/scripts/seed-db.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":15651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1574,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3uzCzrC4cut7RY3uYSZ3w","session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b","uuid":"1d13c1f8-ae25-45f7-8d12-ccfc7325e97c"}
[2026-03-14T20:56:46.859Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTUdsbLy38mamUUT1Ythyt","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# seed-db\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Seeds the database with initial data. The seed script lives at `scripts/seed-db.ts` in each app.\n     6→\n     7→## Usage\n     8→\n     9→```bash\n    10→npx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts\n    11→```\n    12→\n    13→## Known Issues\n    14→\n    15→### Existing data causes failures\n    16→\n    17→The seed script may fail if data already exists in the database (e.g., duplicate key errors).\n    18→This happens when re-seeding after a previous run or when Neon branches inherit parent data.\n    19→\n    20→**Workaround**: Clear existing data before re-seeding:\n    21→\n    22→```sql\n    23→-- Run via npx tsx -e or a cleanup script\n    24→TRUNCATE table1, table2, table3 CASCADE;\n    25→```\n    26→\n    27→Then re-run the seed script.\n    28→\n    29→### Best practice\n    30→\n    31→Seed scripts should always call `truncateAllTables()` (or equivalent) before inserting data\n    32→to ensure idempotency. If the app's seed script does not do this, consider adding a\n    33→`--clean` or `--force` flag that truncates all tables before seeding.\n    34→\n    35→### Pre-test re-seeding\n    36→\n    37→Always re-seed the database before running test suites to ensure a clean, known state. The\n    38→test script (`npm run test`) handles this automatically via ephemeral Neon branches with\n    39→truncate-and-seed between each test. If running tests manually or debugging, re-seed\n    40→explicitly:\n    41→\n    42→```bash\n    43→npx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts\n    44→```\n    45→\n    46→This eliminates the #2 source of test failures (data contamination from accumulated state).\n    47→\n    48→### When to use `scripts/seed-db.ts` vs `/api/seed`\n    49→\n    50→- **`npx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts`**: Use for initial database setup, manual re-seeding before\n    51→  test runs, and when the dev server is not running. Runs directly against the database.\n    52→- **`POST /api/seed` endpoint**: Use inside test `beforeEach`/`beforeAll` hooks to reset\n    53→  state between tests while the dev server is running. This is the preferred approach for\n    54→  in-test reseeding because it uses the same database connection as the running server and\n    55→  avoids connection conflicts. Many test failures trace back to stale seed data — using the\n    56→  `/api/seed` endpoint in `beforeEach` hooks is the most effective mitigation.\n    57→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3uzCzrC4cut7RY3uYSZ3w","session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b","uuid":"643468c4-3f1d-4215-a126-7d483908b13b"}
[2026-03-14T20:56:46.859Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPT88JVm2p7PeCZjxGi77W","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { execSync, spawn } from 'child_process'\n     2→import { writeFileSync, readFileSync, mkdirSync, readdirSync, existsSync } from 'fs'\n     3→import { join } from 'path'\n     4→import { initSchema } from './schema.js'\n     5→import { seedDatabase, resetDatabase } from './seed-db.js'\n     6→\n     7→const appDir = join(import.meta.dirname, '..')\n     8→const logsDir = join(appDir, 'logs')\n     9→\n    10→function getEnvVar(name: string): string {\n    11→  const val = process.env[name]\n    12→  if (!val) {\n    13→    console.error(`Missing required environment variable: ${name}`)\n    14→    process.exit(1)\n    15→  }\n    16→  return val\n    17→}\n    18→\n    19→function loadDotEnv(): void {\n    20→  const envPath = join(appDir, '.env')\n    21→  if (!existsSync(envPath)) return\n    22→  const lines = readFileSync(envPath, 'utf-8').split('\\n')\n    23→  for (const line of lines) {\n    24→    const trimmed = line.trim()\n    25→    if (!trimmed || trimmed.startsWith('#')) continue\n    26→    const eqIdx = trimmed.indexOf('=')\n    27→    if (eqIdx === -1) continue\n    28→    const key = trimmed.slice(0, eqIdx).trim()\n    29→    const value = trimmed.slice(eqIdx + 1).trim().replace(/^[\"']|[\"']$/g, '')\n    30→    if (!process.env[key]) {\n    31→      process.env[key] = value\n    32→    }\n    33→  }\n    34→}\n    35→\n    36→function getNextLogNumber(): number {\n    37→  mkdirSync(logsDir, { recursive: true })\n    38→  const existing = readdirSync(logsDir)\n    39→    .filter(f => /^test-run-\\d+\\.log$/.test(f))\n    40→    .map(f => parseInt(f.match(/test-run-(\\d+)\\.log/)![1]!, 10))\n    41→  return existing.length > 0 ? Math.max(...existing) + 1 : 1\n    42→}\n    43→\n    44→function killStaleProcesses(): void {\n    45→  try { execSync(\"pkill -f 'netlify dev' || true\", { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n    46→  try { execSync(\"pkill -f 'vite' || true\", { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n    47→  execSync('sleep 1', { stdio: 'ignore' })\n    48→}\n    49→\n    50→async function neonApi(method: string, path: string, body?: unknown): Promise<unknown> {\n    51→  const apiKey = getEnvVar('NEON_API_KEY')\n    52→  const res = await fetch(`https://console.neon.tech/api/v2${path}`, {\n    53→    method,\n    54→    headers: {\n    55→      Authorization: `Bearer ${apiKey}`,\n    56→      'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    57→      Accept: 'application/json',\n    58→    },\n    59→    body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined,\n    60→  })\n    61→  if (!res.ok) {\n    62→    const text = await res.text()\n    63→    throw new Error(`Neon API ${method} ${path} failed (${res.status}): ${text}`)\n    64→  }\n    65→  const ct = res.headers.get('content-type')\n    66→  if (ct?.includes('application/json')) return res.json()\n    67→  return null\n    68→}\n    69→\n    70→interface NeonBranch { id: string; name: string }\n    71→interface NeonBranchListResponse { branches: NeonBranch[] }\n    72→interface NeonEndpoint { host: string }\n    73→interface NeonEndpointsResponse { endpoints: NeonEndpoint[] }\n    74→interface NeonBranchCreateResponse { branch: NeonBranch; endpoints: NeonEndpoint[] }\n    75→\n    76→async function cleanupStaleBranches(projectId: string): Promise<void> {\n    77→  const data = await neonApi('GET', `/projects/${projectId}/branches`) as NeonBranchListResponse\n    78→  const stale = data.branches.filter(b => b.name.startsWith('test-run-'))\n    79→  for (const branch of stale) {\n    80→    try { await neonApi('DELETE', `/projects/${projectId}/branches/${branch.id}`) } catch { /* best effort */ }\n    81→  }\n    82→}\n    83→\n    84→async function createEphemeralBranch(projectId: string, branchName: string): Promise<string> {\n    85→  const data = await neonApi('POST', `/projects/${projectId}/branches`, {\n    86→    branch: { name: branchName },\n    87→    endpoints: [{ type: 'read_write' }],\n    88→  }) as NeonBranchCreateResponse\n    89→\n    90→  let host = data.endpoints[0]?.host\n    91→  if (!host) {\n    92→    const epData = await neonApi('GET', `/projects/${projectId}/branches/${data.branch.id}/endpoints`) as NeonEndpointsResponse\n    93→    host = epData.endpoints[0]?.host\n    94→    if (!host) throw new Error('No endpoint created for ephemeral branch')\n    95→  }\n    96→  const mainDbUrl = getEnvVar('DATABASE_URL')\n    97→  const url = new URL(mainDbUrl)\n    98→  url.hostname = host\n    99→  return url.toString()\n   100→}\n   101→\n   102→async function deleteBranch(projectId: string, branchName: string): Promise<void> {\n   103→  const data = await neonApi('GET', `/projects/${projectId}/branches`) as NeonBranchListResponse\n   104→  const branch = data.branches.find(b => b.name === branchName)\n   105→  if (branch) {\n   106→    await neonApi('DELETE', `/projects/${projectId}/branches/${branch.id}`)\n   107→  }\n   108→}\n   109→\n   110→interface RecordingEntry {\n   111→  id?: string; kind: string; metadata?: { test?: { result?: string; title?: string }; uri?: string }; duration?: number\n   112→}\n   113→interface ParsedRecording { id: string; testResult: string; testTitle: string; specFile: string; duration: number }\n   114→\n   115→function parseRecordingsLog(): ParsedRecording[] {\n   116→  const logPath = join(process.env.HOME || '~', '.replay', 'recordings.log')\n   117→  if (!existsSync(logPath)) return []\n   118→  const content = readFileSync(logPath, 'utf-8')\n   119→  const lines = content.split('\\n').filter(l => l.trim())\n   120→  const recordings = new Map<string, { id: string; duration: number }>()\n   121→  const metadata = new Map<string, { testResult: string; testTitle: string; specFile: string }>()\n   122→  for (const line of lines) {\n   123→    try {\n   124→      const entry = JSON.parse(line) as RecordingEntry\n   125→      if (entry.kind === 'createRecording' && entry.id) recordings.set(entry.id, { id: entry.id, duration: 0 })\n   126→      if (entry.kind === 'writeFinished' && entry.id) {\n   127→        const rec = recordings.get(entry.id)\n   128→        if (rec && entry.duration) rec.duration = entry.duration\n   129→      }\n   130→      if (entry.kind === 'addMetadata' && entry.id && entry.metadata?.test) {\n   131→        metadata.set(entry.id, {\n   132→          testResult: entry.metadata.test.result || 'unknown',\n   133→          testTitle: entry.metadata.test.title || '',\n   134→          specFile: entry.metadata.uri || '',\n   135→        })\n   136→      }\n   137→    } catch { /* skip */ }\n   138→  }\n   139→  const results: ParsedRecording[] = []\n   140→  for (const [id, rec] of recordings) {\n   141→    const meta = metadata.get(id)\n   142→    if (meta) results.push({ id, ...meta, duration: rec.duration })\n   143→  }\n   144→  return results\n   145→}\n   146→\n   147→async function main(): Promise<void> {\n   148→  loadDotEnv()\n   149→  const testFile = process.argv[2]\n   150→  if (!testFile) { console.error('Usage: npm run test <testFile>'); process.exit(1) }\n   151→\n   152→  const projectId = getEnvVar('NEON_PROJECT_ID')\n   153→  getEnvVar('DATABASE_URL')\n   154→\n   155→  const logNum = getNextLogNumber()\n   156→  const logFile = join(logsDir, `test-run-${logNum}.log`)\n   157→  const branchName = `test-run-${Date.now()}`\n   158→  let playwrightExitCode = 1\n   159→  let ephemeralDbUrl = ''\n   160→\n   161→  killStaleProcesses()\n   162→  await cleanupStaleBranches(projectId)\n   163→\n   164→  try {\n   165→    ephemeralDbUrl = await createEphemeralBranch(projectId, branchName)\n   166→  } catch (err) {\n   167→    console.error(`Failed to create ephemeral branch: ${err}`)\n   168→    process.exit(1)\n   169→  }\n   170→\n   171→  try {\n   172→    await initSchema(ephemeralDbUrl)\n   173→    await seedDatabase(ephemeralDbUrl)\n   174→\n   175→    const netlifyDev = spawn('npx', ['netlify', 'dev', '--port', '8888', '--functions', './netlify/functions'], {\n   176→      cwd: appDir,\n   177→      env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl },\n   178→      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n   179→      detached: true,\n   180→    })\n   181→\n   182→    await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {\n   183→      const timeout = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('netlify dev failed to start within 60s')), 60000)\n   184→      let output = ''\n   185→      const check = (data: Buffer) => {\n   186→        output += data.toString()\n   187→        if (output.includes('Server ready') || output.includes('ready on') || output.includes('localhost:8888')) {\n   188→          clearTimeout(timeout); resolve()\n   189→        }\n   190→      }\n   191→      netlifyDev.stdout?.on('data', check)\n   192→      netlifyDev.stderr?.on('data', check)\n   193→      netlifyDev.on('error', (err) => { clearTimeout(timeout); reject(err) })\n   194→      netlifyDev.on('exit', (code) => {\n   195→        if (code !== null && code !== 0) { clearTimeout(timeout); reject(new Error(`netlify dev exited ${code}\\n${output}`)) }\n   196→      })\n   197→    })\n   198→\n   199→    try { execSync('npx replayio remove --all', { cwd: appDir, stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n   200→\n   201→    await resetDatabase(ephemeralDbUrl)\n   202→\n   203→    try {\n   204→      const pwOutput = execSync(`npx playwright test ${testFile} --retries 0 --workers 1`, {\n   205→        cwd: appDir, encoding: 'utf-8', stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n   206→        env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl, TEST_DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl, BASE_URL: 'http://localhost:8888' },\n   207→        timeout: 300000,\n   208→      })\n   209→      writeFileSync(logFile, pwOutput)\n   210→      playwrightExitCode = 0\n   211→    } catch (e: unknown) {\n   212→      const err = e as { stdout?: string; stderr?: string; status?: number }\n   213→      writeFileSync(logFile, (err.stdout || '') + '\\n' + (err.stderr || ''))\n   214→      playwrightExitCode = err.status || 1\n   215→    }\n   216→\n   217→    let passed = 0, failed = 0, skipped = 0\n   218→    const resultsPath = join(appDir, 'test-results', 'results.json')\n   219→    if (existsSync(resultsPath)) {\n   220→      try {\n   221→        const rj = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resultsPath, 'utf-8'))\n   222→        for (const suite of rj.suites || []) {\n   223→          for (const spec of suite.specs || []) {\n   224→            for (const test of spec.tests || []) {\n   225→              if (test.status === 'expected' || test.status === 'passed') passed++\n   226→              else if (test.status === 'unexpected' || test.status === 'failed') failed++\n   227→              else if (test.status === 'skipped') skipped++\n   228→            }\n   229→          }\n   230→        }\n   231→      } catch { /* ignore */ }\n   232→    }\n   233→\n   234→    let uploadedId = ''\n   235→    if (playwrightExitCode !== 0) {\n   236→      const recs = parseRecordingsLog()\n   237→      if (recs.length > 0) {\n   238→        let block = '\\n=== REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\\n'\n   239→        for (const r of recs) block += JSON.stringify({ id: r.id, testResult: r.testResult, testTitle: r.testTitle, specFile: r.specFile }) + '\\n'\n   240→        block += '=== END REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\\n'\n   241→        writeFileSync(logFile, readFileSync(logFile, 'utf-8') + block)\n   242→      }\n   243→      const failedRecs = recs.filter(r => r.testResult === 'failed' || r.testResult === 'timedOut').sort((a, b) => b.duration - a.duration)\n   244→      if (failedRecs[0]) {\n   245→        try {\n   246→          execSync(`npx replayio upload ${failedRecs[0].id}`, { cwd: appDir, encoding: 'utf-8', stdio: 'pipe', timeout: 120000 })\n   247→          uploadedId = failedRecs[0].id\n   248→          writeFileSync(logFile, readFileSync(logFile, 'utf-8') + `\\nREPLAY UPLOADED: ${uploadedId}\\n`)\n   249→        } catch (e: unknown) {\n   250→          const err = e as { status?: number }\n   251→          writeFileSync(logFile, readFileSync(logFile, 'utf-8') + `\\nREPLAY UPLOAD FAILED (exit code ${err.status || 'unknown'})\\n`)\n   252→        }\n   253→      }\n   254→    }\n   255→\n   256→    try { if (netlifyDev.pid) process.kill(-netlifyDev.pid, 'SIGTERM') } catch { /* ignore */ }\n   257→\n   258→    const parts: string[] = []\n   259→    if (passed > 0) parts.push(`${passed} passed`)\n   260→    if (failed > 0) parts.push(`${failed} failed`)\n   261→    if (skipped > 0) parts.push(`${skipped} skipped`)\n   262→    let summary = parts.length > 0 ? parts.join(', ') : (playwrightExitCode === 0 ? 'all passed' : 'tests failed')\n   263→    if (uploadedId) summary += ` (recording: ${uploadedId})`\n   264→    if (playwrightExitCode !== 0) summary += ` — see logs/test-run-${logNum}.log`\n   265→    console.log(summary)\n   266→\n   267→  } finally {\n   268→    try { await deleteBranch(projectId, branchName) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n   269→    try { execSync('npx replayio remove --all', { cwd: appDir, stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n   270→    killStaleProcesses()\n   271→  }\n   272→\n   273→  process.exit(playwrightExitCode)\n   274→}\n   275→\n   276→main()\n   277→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1df8f68e-c3f5-4476-ab07-9c768497602b","uuid":"fabaf8b6-3bed-43cc-8318-2aa2f9fcc4c1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/test.ts","content":"import { execSync, spawn } from 'child_process'\nimport { writeFileSync, readFileSync, mkdirSync, readdirSync, existsSync } from 'fs'\nimport { join } from 'path'\nimport { initSchema } from './schema.js'\nimport { seedDatabase, resetDatabase } from './seed-db.js'\n\nconst appDir = join(import.meta.dirname, '..')\nconst logsDir = join(appDir, 'logs')\n\nfunction getEnvVar(name: string): string {\n  const val = process.env[name]\n  if (!val) {\n    console.error(`Missing required environment variable: ${name}`)\n    process.exit(1)\n  }\n  return val\n}\n\nfunction loadDotEnv(): void {\n  const envPath = join(appDir, '.env')\n  if (!existsSync(envPath)) return\n  const lines = readFileSync(envPath, 'utf-8').split('\\n')\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    const trimmed = line.trim()\n    if (!trimmed || trimmed.startsWith('#')) continue\n    const eqIdx = trimmed.indexOf('=')\n    if (eqIdx === -1) continue\n    const key = trimmed.slice(0, eqIdx).trim()\n    const value = trimmed.slice(eqIdx + 1).trim().replace(/^[\"']|[\"']$/g, '')\n    if (!process.env[key]) {\n      process.env[key] = value\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction getNextLogNumber(): number {\n  mkdirSync(logsDir, { recursive: true })\n  const existing = readdirSync(logsDir)\n    .filter(f => /^test-run-\\d+\\.log$/.test(f))\n    .map(f => parseInt(f.match(/test-run-(\\d+)\\.log/)![1]!, 10))\n  return existing.length > 0 ? Math.max(...existing) + 1 : 1\n}\n\nfunction killStaleProcesses(): void {\n  try { execSync(\"pkill -f 'netlify dev' || true\", { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n  try { execSync(\"pkill -f 'vite' || true\", { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n  execSync('sleep 1', { stdio: 'ignore' })\n}\n\nasync function neonApi(method: string, path: string, body?: unknown): Promise<unknown> {\n  const apiKey = getEnvVar('NEON_API_KEY')\n  const res = await fetch(`https://console.neon.tech/api/v2${path}`, {\n    method,\n    headers: {\n      Authorization: `Bearer ${apiKey}`,\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n      Accept: 'application/json',\n    },\n    body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined,\n  })\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    const text = await res.text()\n    throw new Error(`Neon API ${method} ${path} failed (${res.status}): ${text}`)\n  }\n  const ct = res.headers.get('content-type')\n  if (ct?.includes('application/json')) return res.json()\n  return null\n}\n\ninterface NeonBranch { id: string; name: string }\ninterface NeonBranchListResponse { branches: NeonBranch[] }\ninterface NeonEndpoint { host: string }\ninterface NeonEndpointsResponse { endpoints: NeonEndpoint[] }\ninterface NeonBranchCreateResponse { branch: NeonBranch; endpoints: NeonEndpoint[] }\n\nasync function cleanupStaleBranches(projectId: string): Promise<void> {\n  const data = await neonApi('GET', `/projects/${projectId}/branches`) as NeonBranchListResponse\n  const stale = data.branches.filter(b => b.name.startsWith('test-run-'))\n  for (const branch of stale) {\n    try { await neonApi('DELETE', `/projects/${projectId}/branches/${branch.id}`) } catch { /* best effort */ }\n  }\n}\n\nasync function createEphemeralBranch(projectId: string, branchName: string): Promise<string> {\n  const data = await neonApi('POST', `/projects/${projectId}/branches`, {\n    branch: { name: branchName },\n    endpoints: [{ type: 'read_write' }],\n  }) as NeonBranchCreateResponse\n\n  let host = data.endpoints[0]?.host\n  if (!host) {\n    const epData = await neonApi('GET', `/projects/${projectId}/branches/${data.branch.id}/endpoints`) as NeonEndpointsResponse\n    host = epData.endpoints[0]?.host\n    if (!host) throw new Error('No endpoint created for ephemeral branch')\n  }\n  const mainDbUrl = getEnvVar('DATABASE_URL')\n  const url = new URL(mainDbUrl)\n  url.hostname = host\n  return url.toString()\n}\n\nasync function deleteBranch(projectId: string, branchName: string): Promise<void> {\n  const data = await neonApi('GET', `/projects/${projectId}/branches`) as NeonBranchListResponse\n  const branch = data.branches.find(b => b.name === branchName)\n  if (branch) {\n    await neonApi('DELETE', `/projects/${projectId}/branches/${branch.id}`)\n  }\n}\n\ninterface RecordingEntry {\n  id?: string; kind: string; metadata?: { test?: { result?: string; title?: string }; uri?: string }; duration?: number\n}\ninterface ParsedRecording { id: string; testResult: string; testTitle: string; specFile: string; duration: number }\n\nfunction parseRecordingsLog(): ParsedRecording[] {\n  const logPath = join(process.env.HOME || '~', '.replay', 'recordings.log')\n  if (!existsSync(logPath)) return []\n  const content = readFileSync(logPath, 'utf-8')\n  const lines = content.split('\\n').filter(l => l.trim())\n  const recordings = new Map<string, { id: string; duration: number }>()\n  const metadata = new Map<string, { testResult: string; testTitle: string; specFile: string }>()\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    try {\n      const entry = JSON.parse(line) as RecordingEntry\n      if (entry.kind === 'createRecording' && entry.id) recordings.set(entry.id, { id: entry.id, duration: 0 })\n      if (entry.kind === 'writeFinished' && entry.id) {\n        const rec = recordings.get(entry.id)\n        if (rec && entry.duration) rec.duration = entry.duration\n      }\n      if (entry.kind === 'addMetadata' && entry.id && entry.metadata?.test) {\n        metadata.set(entry.id, {\n          testResult: entry.metadata.test.result || 'unknown',\n          testTitle: entry.metadata.test.title || '',\n          specFile: entry.metadata.uri || '',\n        })\n      }\n    } catch { /* skip */ }\n  }\n  const results: ParsedRecording[] = []\n  for (const [id, rec] of recordings) {\n    const meta = metadata.get(id)\n    if (meta) results.push({ id, ...meta, duration: rec.duration })\n  }\n  return results\n}\n\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  loadDotEnv()\n  const testFile = process.argv[2]\n  if (!testFile) { console.error('Usage: npm run test <testFile>'); process.exit(1) }\n\n  const projectId = getEnvVar('NEON_PROJECT_ID')\n  getEnvVar('DATABASE_URL')\n\n  const logNum = getNextLogNumber()\n  const logFile = join(logsDir, `test-run-${logNum}.log`)\n  const branchName = `test-run-${Date.now()}`\n  let playwrightExitCode = 1\n  let ephemeralDbUrl = ''\n\n  killStaleProcesses()\n  await cleanupStaleBranches(projectId)\n\n  try {\n    ephemeralDbUrl = await createEphemeralBranch(projectId, branchName)\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(`Failed to create ephemeral branch: ${err}`)\n    process.exit(1)\n  }\n\n  try {\n    await initSchema(ephemeralDbUrl)\n    await seedDatabase(ephemeralDbUrl)\n\n    const netlifyDev = spawn('npx', ['netlify', 'dev', '--port', '8888', '--functions', './netlify/functions'], {\n      cwd: appDir,\n      env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl },\n      stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n      detached: true,\n    })\n\n    await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {\n      const timeout = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('netlify dev failed to start within 60s')), 60000)\n      let output = ''\n      const check = (data: Buffer) => {\n        output += data.toString()\n        if (output.includes('Server ready') || output.includes('ready on') || output.includes('localhost:8888')) {\n          clearTimeout(timeout); resolve()\n        }\n      }\n      netlifyDev.stdout?.on('data', check)\n      netlifyDev.stderr?.on('data', check)\n      netlifyDev.on('error', (err) => { clearTimeout(timeout); reject(err) })\n      netlifyDev.on('exit', (code) => {\n        if (code !== null && code !== 0) { clearTimeout(timeout); reject(new Error(`netlify dev exited ${code}\\n${output}`)) }\n      })\n    })\n\n    try { execSync('npx replayio remove --all', { cwd: appDir, stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n\n    await resetDatabase(ephemeralDbUrl)\n\n    try {\n      const pwOutput = execSync(`npx playwright test ${testFile} --retries 0 --workers 1`, {\n        cwd: appDir, encoding: 'utf-8', stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n        env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl, TEST_DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl, BASE_URL: 'http://localhost:8888' },\n        timeout: 300000,\n      })\n      writeFileSync(logFile, pwOutput)\n      playwrightExitCode = 0\n    } catch (e: unknown) {\n      const err = e as { stdout?: string; stderr?: string; status?: number }\n      writeFileSync(logFile, (err.stdout || '') + '\\n' + (err.stderr || ''))\n      playwrightExitCode = err.status || 1\n    }\n\n    let passed = 0, failed = 0, skipped = 0\n    const resultsPath = join(appDir, 'test-results', 'results.json')\n    if (existsSync(resultsPath)) {\n      try {\n        const rj = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resultsPath, 'utf-8'))\n        for (const suite of rj.suites || []) {\n          for (const spec of suite.specs || []) {\n            for (const test of spec.tests || []) {\n              if (test.status === 'expected' || test.status === 'passed') passed++\n              else if (test.status === 'unexpected' || test.status === 'failed') failed++\n              else if (test.status === 'skipped') skipped++\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      } catch { /* ignore */ }\n    }\n\n    let uploadedId = ''\n    if (playwrightExitCode !== 0) {\n      const recs = parseRecordingsLog()\n      if (recs.length > 0) {\n        let block = '\\n=== REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\\n'\n        for (const r of recs) block += JSON.stringify({ id: r.id, testResult: r.testResult, testTitle: r.testTitle, specFile: r.specFile }) + '\\n'\n        block += '=== END REPLAY RECORDINGS METADATA ===\\n'\n        writeFileSync(logFile, readFileSync(logFile, 'utf-8') + block)\n      }\n      const failedRecs = recs.filter(r => r.testResult === 'failed' || r.testResult === 'timedOut').sort((a, b) => b.duration - a.duration)\n      if (failedRecs[0]) {\n        try {\n          execSync(`npx replayio upload ${failedRecs[0].id}`, { cwd: appDir, encoding: 'utf-8', stdio: 'pipe', timeout: 120000 })\n          uploadedId = failedRecs[0].id\n          writeFileSync(logFile, readFileSync(logFile, 'utf-8') + `\\nREPLAY UPLOADED: ${uploadedId}\\n`)\n        } catch (e: unknown) {\n          const err = e as { status?: number }\n          writeFileSync(logFile, readFileSync(logFile, 'utf-8') + `\\nREPLAY UPLOAD FAILED (exit code ${err.status || 'unknown'})\\n`)\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    try { if (netlifyDev.pid) process.kill(-netlifyDev.pid, 'SIGTERM') } catch { /* ignore */ }\n\n    const parts: string[] = []\n    if (passed > 0) parts.push(`${passed} passed`)\n    if (failed > 0) parts.push(`${failed} failed`)\n    if (skipped > 0) parts.push(`${skipped} skipped`)\n    let summary = parts.length > 0 ? parts.join(', ') : (playwrightExitCode === 0 ? 'all passed' : 'tests failed')\n    if (uploadedId) summary += ` (recording: ${uploadedId})`\n    if (playwrightExitCode !== 0) summary += ` — see logs/test-run-${logNum}.log`\n    console.log(summary)\n\n  } finally {\n    try { await deleteBranch(projectId, branchName) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n    try { execSync('npx replayio remove --all', { cwd: appDir, stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n    killStaleProcesses()\n  }\n\n  process.exit(playwrightExitCode)\n}\n\nmain()\n","numLines":277,"startLine":1,"totalLines":277}}}
